  "text": "Listening to Papers: A Field Study\n\nAda Example¹, Ben Sample²\n\n¹ Example University ² Sample Institute\n\nAbstract\n\nWe asked twelve researchers to listen to papers on their commute.\n\n1 Introduction\n\nListening is slower than reading [3], but it fits into time that reading cannot use.¹ Figure 1 shows when participants listened.\n\n¹ Commutes, walks and chores.\n\nProc. Example Conf. 2026 · 1\n\nListening to Papers\n\nFigure 1: Listening sessions by hour of day.\n\nTable 1: Sessions per participant.\n\nParticipant Sessions P1 14 P2 9\n\nMost sessions happened before 9 a.m. The energy E = mc² of a morning commute is, of course, a metaphor.\n\nReferences\n\n[3] C. Writer. Reading and listening. J. Examples, 2020.",
